---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../../content/site';
import { pages } from '../../content/pages';

const sections: [string, string][] = [
  ['overview', 'Program overview'],
  ['eligibility', 'Eligibility and selection'],
  ['structure', 'Program structure'],
  ['standards', 'Technical standards'],
  ['conduct', 'Code of conduct'],
  ['attendance', 'Attendance and communication'],
  ['evaluation', 'Evaluation and certification'],
  ['termination', 'Leaving the program early'],
];
const crumbs = [{ name: 'Internship', path: '/internship' }, { name: 'Course guidelines', path: '/internship/guidelines' }];
---
<Legal
  page={pages.guidelines}
  name="Internship course guidelines"
  label="Internship"
  crumbs={crumbs}
  sections={sections}
  effective=""
  summary={[
    'One to three months of hands-on work on live project code, remote or hybrid.',
    'At least 20 hours a week, with stand-ups, weekly reviews and code walkthroughs.',
    'Certificates go to interns who score 70% or above in the final evaluation.',
    'Plagiarism, breaking confidentiality or repeated absence ends the internship without a certificate.',
  ]}
>
    <h2 id="overview">1. Program overview</h2>
    <p>The Dremora IT Internship Program is hands-on training for students who want to become software developers or designers. Interns work on live project code and build features that real users rely on.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Duration:</strong> 1 to 3 months, depending on the project</li>
      <li><strong>Mode:</strong> remote or hybrid. Candidates in Pune can choose to work on-site.</li>
      <li><strong>Stipend:</strong> performance-based, explained during onboarding</li>
      <li><strong>Certificate:</strong> issued when the program is completed successfully</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="eligibility">2. Eligibility and selection</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You are enrolled in, or have completed, a degree or diploma in Computer Science, IT, Engineering, Design or a related field.</li>
      <li>You have at least basic knowledge of programming (any language), web development or UI design.</li>
      <li>You can commit to the agreed hours, at least 20 hours a week.</li>
      <li>You complete a short technical task or portfolio review as part of selection.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Selection is on merit. We look at problem solving, attitude to learning and communication, not only technical scores.</p>

    <h2 id="structure">3. Program structure</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Onboarding (week 1):</strong> our tech stack, tools, workflow and project code. You set up your development environment and finish orientation tasks.</li>
      <li><strong>Core development (weeks 2 to 8):</strong> assigned features, modules or projects under a mentor, with weekly reviews and code walkthroughs.</li>
      <li><strong>Capstone and review (final 2 weeks):</strong> a capstone module, peer reviews and a presentation of your work to the team.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2 id="standards">4. Technical standards</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Write clean, readable code with comments where they help, following our coding conventions.</li>
      <li>Use Git for all work, with clear commit messages.</li>
      <li>Review your own work before you submit a pull request or deliverable.</li>
      <li>Attend all scheduled technical reviews and stand-up meetings.</li>
      <li>Test your code before submitting it. Untested code is sent back for revision.</li>
      <li>Never push directly to the main branch without your mentor's approval.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="conduct">5. Code of conduct</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Treat team members, mentors and clients with respect at all times.</li>
      <li>Keep internal projects, client data and business information confidential.</li>
      <li>Be honest about progress. If you are stuck, say so early.</li>
      <li>Do not plagiarise. All code and design must be your own or properly credited.</li>
      <li>Do not share passwords, internal documents or project files with anyone outside the team.</li>
      <li>Report issues, conflicts or concerns to your mentor or the program lead promptly.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="attendance">6. Attendance and communication</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Attend at least 80% of scheduled meetings and check-ins.</li>
      <li>Tell your mentor at least 24 hours in advance if you cannot attend a session.</li>
      <li>Reply on official channels (WhatsApp, Slack or email) within 4 working hours on business days.</li>
      <li>Post a daily stand-up update in the intern group: what you did, what you plan next, and anything blocking you.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="evaluation">7. Evaluation and certification</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Area</th><th scope="col">Weight</th><th scope="col">What it covers</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Technical quality</td><td class="mono">40%</td><td>Code quality, problem solving and technical understanding</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Project contribution</td><td class="mono">30%</td><td>Features built, bugs fixed and work delivered</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Professionalism</td><td class="mono">20%</td><td>Punctuality, communication, teamwork and conduct</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Learning and growth</td><td class="mono">10%</td><td>Visible improvement from start to end</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>Interns who score 70% or above receive a completion certificate and a letter of recommendation. Strong performers may be offered an extended or full-time role. Every certificate can be checked on the <a href="/internship#verify">certificate check</a>.</p>

    <h2 id="termination">8. Leaving the program early</h2>
    <p>We may end an intern's participation for:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>repeated breaches of the code of conduct</li>
      <li>continued absence or no response without a valid reason</li>
      <li>breach of confidentiality</li>
      <li>plagiarism, dishonesty or submitting copied work</li>
    </ul>
    <p>In these cases no certificate is issued and access to internal systems is removed at once. Program fees and refunds are covered by the <a href="/refund-policy">Refund Policy</a>.</p>

    <p style="margin-top: 48px">Questions about the program? Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
</Legal>
